===2026, "Digital Series"===

In response to the increasing digitization of the Sanese economy and to combat counterfeiting, the Bank of Okaiken announced the "Digital Series" of banknotes, with a scheduled release beginning in early 2026. This series is the first to be printed entirely on an advanced, durable polymer substrate and features a modern vertical orientation.

A key design change is a reduction in the banknote's length to 68 × 150&nbsp;mm to save on material costs and to fit more easily into modern wallets and cash-handling machines. The portraits of all figures have been updated to high-resolution, front-facing intaglio engravings.

The series introduces a multi-layered security concept based on global standards:
* '''Advanced Polymer Substrate:''' The notes are printed on a smooth, durable polymer that is resistant to tearing and water.
* '''Dual Holographic Features:''' The notes feature two distinct, advanced holographic elements:
** A large, complex '''Transparent Window''' in the upper section, which is a clear part of the polymer. It contains a holographic patch featuring the Okaiken crest and repeating denomination numerals (e.g., '5000').
** A separate '''3D Holographic Portrait Patch''' on the lower half of the note, which shows a three-dimensional, shifting image of the main portrait.
* '''Tactile Intaglio Print:''' The main portraits, large numerals, and key text (like "IMPERIAL KINGDOM OF OKAIKEN") are printed with raised ink, creating a distinct texture that is identifiable by touch and aids the visually impaired.
* '''EURion Constellation:''' A pattern of small circles (visible on the 5000 En note) is integrated into the background design to prevent unauthorized digital copying by high-end scanners and photocopiers.
* '''Dual Serial Numbers:''' Each note features two unique serial numbers in different orientations (one vertical and one horizontal) to enhance security and tracking.
* '''Micro-text:''' Extremely small text, such as "BANK OF OKAIKEN" and the figure's name, is integrated into the portrait's clothing, background patterns, and border designs, visible only under magnification.
* '''UV Fluorescence:''' Elements on both the obverse and reverse, invisible in normal light, fluoresce brightly in one or more colors under ultraviolet light.

